# V29 hook: "Done." (written 2026-10-13)

## Inputs
- V28c (the user said "really nice — push it").
- Two external critiques (pasted 2026-10-13). They agree on these points:
  - Open on the consequence, not on a blank chatbot.
  - Make **"Done"** a motif with its own sound, repeated three times, until it irritates.
  - Add an almost-disaster: the cursor over Send, with the mismatch visible.
  - The breaking point is **silence**, not another clock.
  - Bridge into the product with the black-box line, not the generic question.
  - Fewer progress bars.

**What we kept from V28c:**
- the realistic, unbranded chat, Word, Excel, PowerPoint and PDF windows
- "Five minutes. For one number."
- "Copy. Paste. Check. Repeat."

**What's new:**
- **Real footage, ranked by CLIP** from free stock (Mixkit, Coverr, Wikimedia): night office, phone, hands, face and clock.
- It's intercut with the screens so the story has a person and a place.

## Beats
| # | t (s) | Picture | VO / super | Sound |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 0–4.2 | **Cold open, the consequence.** A phone lights up on a dark desk (real). Hard cut to an email draft to the partner, with Agreement.docx, Annexure.xlsx and Board_Deck.pptx attached. Two values flash side by side: **Model €74.6m · Deck €71–73m**. | VO k1 "Nine a.m. Board meeting. And the deck doesn't match the model." | Phone buzz, low hit |
| 2 | 4.2–5.4 | Tape-rewind glitch. Super: **SIX HOURS EARLIER** | — | Rewind whoosh |
| 3 | 5.4–9.6 | Real: empty office at night, then hands on the keyboard. The chat, with the prompt typed. | o1 "You ask a chatbot to update an agreement." | Room tone, soft typing |
| 4 | 9.6–11.6 | The chat replies with a giant **Done. ✓** (DONE #1) | VO k3 "It says: done." | **DONE chime #1**, clean |
| 5 | 11.6–14.4 | Word opens and glitches. Flags appear. | o3b "Then you open the file… and the formatting's wrecked." | Glitch, static |
| 6 | 14.4–21.6 | Real: tired face lit by the screen. The partner's email drops in. | o4 + o5f (the email) | Buzz; the jazz dies; the suspense bed starts |
| 7 | 21.6–25.2 | The chat builds the deck. **Done. ✓** (DONE #2). The partner pings that revenue is €74.6m. The ring lands on slide 2. | n1 (shortened by cutting) + n2 "Then one number changes." | **DONE chime #2**, a little louder |
| 8 | 25.2–30.4 | Re-prompt. The wall clock (real) is intercut with the 8:41→8:46 time-lapse. | n3 "Prompt again. Wait again. Five minutes… for one number." | Ticking, heartbeat |
| 9 | 30.4–33.6 | **Done. ✓** (DONE #3). Slide 2 is fixed, but slide 4's chart has changed, ringed in red. | VO k4 "Done. Except now… slide four changed." | **DONE chime #3**, louder and with a slapback echo |
| 10 | 33.6–37.2 | Whip montage of the real apps and real footage (hands, eyes, coffee). | o6 "Five tabs. Copy. Paste. Check. Repeat." | Whooshes, impact |
| 11 | 37.2–42.2 | **Breaking point.** The email draft from the cold open. A partner message: "Are these the final files? The client is waiting." The cursor drifts to **Send**… and stops. | VO k5 "The worst part? You don't even know what's wrong anymore." | **Everything cuts to silence** at the cursor stop; only room tone |
| 12 | 42.2–45.0 | Black. Super: **See exactly what changed. Decide what stays.** | VO k6 (same line) | Silence, then a single soft tone (the Agentic Office identity) |
| → | 45.0 | Splice into V27 at 21.8 s (the Agentic Office card) | | V27 music |

**Claims:** "See exactly what changed. Decide what stays." is accurate, because every edit is a tracked change with accept or reject (the real recording).

## Second-half notes (V27 tail, the colleague's Film22). Not touched yet; next pass.
- Consolidate the supers into three: **It finds · It fixes · You decide**.
- Hold the accept/reject diff longer. It's the climax.
- End on the same three files reconciled, then "AI said it was done. This time, it is." with a different, quieter confirmation sound.
# Decisions carried forward / release gates

User feedback and team screenshots informed these decisions. Private chat screenshots and phone numbers are intentionally not copied; the useful creative decisions are summarized here.

| Topic | Keep / show | Avoid / still confirm |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Main proposition | Word, Excel, PowerPoint formats in one agentic, collaborative professional workspace | Not just a cross-document trick or generic AI chat; no complete Microsoft 365 replacement promise |
| Hook | Three work cards merge, a little breathing space between app names | No PDF-editing promotion; no rushed list; audience copy says work, not project |
| UI | Actual team-provided screenshot/prototype and new authentic recordings | No generative/repainted controls, invented result, fake clicks, or unsupported UI |
| Prompt to deck | One prompt uses memo + forecast; proposed presentation opens in the main UI | Existing source is prototype; real generation capture and shipping confirmation are required |
| Selective edits | Accept or reject individual proposed changes, without whole-document rewrite | Screenshot proves visible controls, not an accepted/rejected result; capture real action |
| Collaboration | Shared document, presence, changes, proposals | Prototype isn't release proof; confirm actual supported interaction |
| Cross-agent | Context sharing, coordinated handoff, proposed next change; human decides | No guaranteed autonomous completion/sending; confirm and record the actual handoff |
| Time saving | Less copying, less rework, less switching to separate AI chats | No fabricated minutes/percentages or competitive benchmark |
| Local files | Files stored on device; agent works inside workspace; no separate manual upload step | Local storage ≠ local inference. Keep “Cloud AI may process document content.” Product team must confirm exact data flow |
| Privacy tone | Subtle sense of continuity/control through local file tree and user review | No shield/cloud-blocked icon, “privacy solved,” “never uploaded,” “whole files never sent,” or “local-only AI” |
| Art direction | Plain stages, typography, graphics, truthful UI; reuse opening card language | No AI-generated people, photographic office/laptop shots, cluttered unrelated effects |
| Audio | Narration plus jazz-like groove, drum rolls, synchronized SFX | YouTube music rights are unknown. Inherited SFX licenses unresolved; OpenArt subscription isn't clearance |
| Workflow | New request: Claude + OpenArt; keep V11 Remotion baseline for continuity | Do not force earlier Remotion-only preference onto the new requested workflow; do not assume a quality ceiling of any framework |

## Public launch gates

Confirm all advertised features ship. Replace/label prototype sequences honestly. Obtain sanitized product recordings and official logo/CTA. Confirm privacy wording against architecture. Clear final VO/music/SFX/model-output usage rights. Check accessibility/readability and audio/video export. This folder is a production handoff, not a release authorization.

